"<p>Nitrobase automatically generates an <strong>OpenAPI 3.1.0</strong> document directly from its Zod-validated API route registry (<code>src/server/api/v1.ts</code>):</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-text\"><span class=\"line\"><span>GET https://&#x3C;your-panel>/api/v1/openapi.json</span></span></code></pre>\n<h2>What the Schema Includes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>All <code>/api/v1</code> paths, HTTP methods, <code>operationId</code>s, and summaries.</li>\n<li>Exact JSON Schema definitions for path parameters and request bodies converted from Zod (<code>z.toJSONSchema</code>).</li>\n<li>Bearer authentication security scheme (<code>bearerFormat: \"nbk_…\"</code>).</li>\n<li>Required permission metadata (<code>x-permission</code>) on every operation.</li>\n<li>Server URL populated from <code>APP_URL</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You can import <code>/api/v1/openapi.json</code> into Postman, Insomnia, Bruno, Scalar, or code generators like <code>openapi-typescript</code> to generate strongly typed API clients.</p>"